                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Let's just go to the TL:DR version:\n\nGood:\nScratches the X-com like itch with a new faster paced feel\nReasonable amounts of customization, cool armor and weapons change actual apprearance(would still like to see more)\nGood Variety of missions, no shortage of missions\nGraphics and sound are above average\nSkill Trees and specialties look promising\n\nBad:\nControl/Command system is weird/not intuitive which can leave your soldiers out in the open and not firing at anyone\nCamera can be an absolute hassle because it is stuck on your soldiers. It can zoom in and out harshly depending on the angle your at and what is behind/above you.\nHealing/Medical care is hard to gauge/understand\nNo in-mission healing mechanic availabe from start, left up to RNJesus from drops until a random soldier with the right class and talent appears in hiring screen\nYour line of sight when tucked in cover is abysmal while enemies can shoot through damn near anything\nSoldiers don't open fire on the enemy automatically unless they are shot which makes no sense unless you're cloaked\n\nOverall:\nI like it and I want it to work/be fun.  I'm hoping the Devs continue working through to really polish the UI/controls.  With further updates I would fersure review and change my rating.",
